From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 14:56:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Optionally give each VM one compute
 allocator descriptor

The shared compute pool (g16_compute_shared_pool=1) lets every compute
unit of a VM allocate from unit 0's UMA page ring, but each unit keeps
its own allocator descriptor and UMA index. The firmware saves the
ring's read and write cursors into the descriptor it retires and
programs the allocator row from the descriptor it binds, so up to 16
saved copies of one ring's cursors disagree, and a stale copy can hand
out a page that is still in use.

macOS gives all compute commands of a context one descriptor, one
submitted counter and one UMA index. While commands are counted ahead
the firmware keeps the row bound; it saves the row into that descriptor
once the context drains.

Add mode 2 to g16_compute_shared_pool: one pool and one allocator
descriptor, counter and UMA index (1) per VM, shared by all its compute
units. The host writes the descriptor once, before the VM's first
compute command is counted, and never restores a per-unit copy. A
command is complete once the descriptor's completed count reaches the
count written at its publication. Because every VM binds index 1, a
compute command goes behind running flights only when all of them
belong to its VM. After an aborted counted command, the VM's later
compute commands fail.

Modes 0 (the default) and 1 are unchanged. The statistics report mode 2
as shared_pool 3.

Assisted-by: LLM
